spec.text:
{
 "id": "T-303",
 "milestone": "M2",
 "depends_on": [
  "T-302"
 ],
 "title": "Every task spec names its door, and the door picks the process: a two-way change skips the plan round and fail-first and its review checks correctness only, a one-way change keeps the full path, and a round that finds the door was wrong stops for a new card",
 "public_title": "Two-way and one-way changes take different paths",
 "door": {
  "kind": "two-way",
  "reason": "Only which checks a task runs changes; a revert restores the single full path."
 },
 "scope": [
  "bin/**",
  "skills/**",
  "tests/**",
  "design/design.md",
  "config.yaml",
  "i18n/**"
 ],
 "acceptance": [
  "Why. Today every change takes the same path: a plan round, a build, fail-first proof, about ten minutes of CI, a full review and six gates, about 30 to 40 minutes end to end, even for a one-word rename that a plain session does in five seconds. On 2026-10-13 the captain set the rule: one-way and two-way door changes take different development paths. A two-way change can be undone by a revert; a one-way change cannot (data formats, deleted data, public interfaces, credentials and permissions, git history).",
  "What, the door is part of the spec. A task spec names its door, two-way or one-way, with a one-line reason. A spec with no door is treated as one-way. The dispatch card shows the door and its reason.",
  "What, sensitive paths force one-way. One list in config names the paths that are always one-way: credentials and permissions (sandbox and hook rules included), data formats and migrations, deletion of data, public interfaces, and git history. A two-way spec is pinned one-way when one of its scope entries itself falls inside a listed path (bin/fm-merge.sh does; a wide entry such as bin/** does not). A two-way task whose diff touches a listed path is handled as one-way at the gates and its pin stops for a new card. The card or gate says which path did it.",
  "What, the two-way path. No plan round: the first round builds. The fail-first gate does not apply. The review checks correctness and scope only (no fail-first, style or migration asks); a REJECT goes back to the worker as today, under the same round budget as a one-way task. CI, the scope gate, the designer review for UI pages, and the merge card stay as today; the captain still approves every merge.",
  "What, the one-way path. Exactly today's path: plan round, fail-first, full review and all six gates. The merge card also states the rollback plan.",
  "What, the door can change. When a round finds evidence that the door is wrong (for example a two-way task needs a data format change), the worker says so in its report and stops; no further round starts on that pin. Firstmate then raises a new card with a revised spec. A task never switches path in the middle of a pin.",
  "What, unchanged. External projects, the merge card, and tasks already pinned before this change keep today's path.",
  "Done, tests. A two-way task's first round builds without a plan (`door: two-way builds first`, fail-first); a one-way task and a task with no door still require the plan (`door: one-way and missing keep the plan`, fail-first); the fail-first gate passes a two-way head without fail-first evidence and still refuses a one-way head (`door: fail-first gate by door`, fail-first); a two-way spec touching a listed sensitive path is handled as one-way and the reason names the path (`door: sensitive path forces one-way`, fail-first); a round report that flags a door change stops the next round on that pin (`door: change stops the task`, fail-first).",
  "Docs. The firstmate, worker and reviewer skills and design.md describe the two paths in a few lines each.",
  "Glossary. i18n/glossary.json gains the term door (two-way or one-way) in every locale, so cards can use the word."
 ],
 "explain": {
  "en": {
   "intent": [
    {
     "kind": "fact",
     "text": "Each spec says two-way or one-way, and a spec that says neither is one-way."
    },
    {
     "kind": "fact",
     "text": "A two-way task skips the plan round and fail-first, and its review checks correctness only."
    },
    {
     "kind": "fact",
     "text": "A listed sensitive path makes a task one-way."
    },
    {
     "kind": "fact",
     "text": "A round that finds the wrong type stops for a new card."
    }
   ],
   "why": [
    {
     "kind": "fact",
     "text": "Every change takes the full path today, even a one-word rename."
    },
    {
     "kind": "fact",
     "text": "On 2026-10-13 the captain set one path for two-way changes and one for one-way changes."
    }
   ],
   "scope_in": [
    "the task spec",
    "the worker launcher",
    "the gates",
    "the review",
    "config"
   ],
   "scope_out": [
    "the merge card",
    "external projects",
    "tasks pinned before this change"
   ],
   "done": [
    {
     "kind": "fact",
     "text": "Intent 1: a test shows a spec with no type keeps the plan round."
    },
    {
     "kind": "fact",
     "text": "Intent 2: a test shows a two-way task builds first and passes without fail-first."
    },
    {
     "kind": "fact",
     "text": "Intent 3: a test shows a sensitive path makes the task one-way."
    },
    {
     "kind": "fact",
     "text": "Intent 4: a test shows a type change stops the next round."
    }
   ],
   "notes": [
    {
     "kind": "note",
     "text": "You still approve every merge on a card."
    }
   ],
   "before_nodes": [
    {
     "state": "same",
     "label": "Dispatch"
    },
    {
     "state": "gone",
     "label": "One full path"
    },
    {
     "state": "same",
     "label": "Merge card"
    }
   ],
   "after_nodes": [
    {
     "state": "same",
     "label": "Dispatch"
    },
    {
     "state": "new",
     "label": "Path by change type"
    },
    {
     "state": "same",
     "label": "Merge card"
    }
   ]
  },
  "zh-TW": {
   "intent": [
    {
     "kind": "fact",
     "text": "每份 spec 寫明 door，沒寫就當 one-way。"
    },
    {
     "kind": "fact",
     "text": "two-way 任務不跑計畫輪和 fail-first，審查只看正確性。"
    },
    {
     "kind": "fact",
     "text": "碰到清單上的敏感路徑，任務改走 one-way。"
    },
    {
     "kind": "fact",
     "text": "某輪發現 door 判斷錯誤，任務停下並開新卡。"
    }
   ],
   "why": [
    {
     "kind": "fact",
     "text": "現在每個改動都走完整流程，改一個字也一樣。"
    },
    {
     "kind": "fact",
     "text": "船長在 2026-10-13 定下兩種 door 各走一條路。"
    }
   ],
   "scope_in": [
    "任務 spec",
    "worker 啟動器",
    "gate",
    "審查",
    "config"
   ],
   "scope_out": [
    "合併卡",
    "外部專案",
    "這次改動前已 pin 的任務"
   ],
   "done": [
    {
     "kind": "fact",
     "text": "意圖 1：測試證明沒寫 door 的 spec 保留計畫輪。"
    },
    {
     "kind": "fact",
     "text": "意圖 2：測試證明 two-way 任務直接實作，不需要 fail-first。"
    },
    {
     "kind": "fact",
     "text": "意圖 3：測試證明敏感路徑讓任務改走 one-way。"
    },
    {
     "kind": "fact",
     "text": "意圖 4：測試證明 door 改變會擋下下一輪。"
    }
   ],
   "notes": [
    {
     "kind": "note",
     "text": "每次合併仍由你在卡片上核准。"
    }
   ],
   "before_nodes": [
    {
     "state": "same",
     "label": "派工"
    },
    {
     "state": "gone",
     "label": "一條完整流程"
    },
    {
     "state": "same",
     "label": "合併卡"
    }
   ],
   "after_nodes": [
    {
     "state": "same",
     "label": "派工"
    },
    {
     "state": "new",
     "label": "依 door 分流程"
    },
    {
     "state": "same",
     "label": "合併卡"
    }
   ]
  }
 }
}
